Introduction

Beacon provides tracking and visibility for shipments created through Navigator as well as shipments originating from external systems. These externally created shipments are referred to as Non-Navigator Shipments or Unverified Data.

Non-Navigator shipments are primarily identified by matching the Bill-to Third-Party Account Number with the Billing Group account number associated with the user's location. This allows Beacon to provide a consolidated view of shipments even when they were not created directly through Navigator.

Key Points

Shipment Identification
Non-Navigator shipments are identified using the Bill-to Third-Party Account Number and the corresponding Billing Group account.

Shipment Visibility
These shipments are displayed along with Navigator-originating shipments in Shipment Tracking and Shipping History.

Include Unverified Data
Users with both Navigator and Beacon access can select Include Unverified Data from the Location dropdown to view these shipments.

Beacon-Only Users
Users who only have Beacon access will not see the Location dropdown and will automatically see the relevant shipment data available to them.

Data Availability
Since these shipments originate outside Navigator, some Navigator-specific fields may be unavailable and can appear as blank or N/A.

External Shipment Data
External data, including Surround data, can provide additional shipment and operational information, especially for Beacon+ customers.

Broader Beacon Capabilities
Non-Navigator shipments can also support features such as POD, notifications, exports, reporting, and data streaming, depending on the shipment type and customer configuration.


