Backend

FedEx Surround Data Flow

The v1/api/surround-tracking-events API is exposed by the Surround Edge Service to receive shipment/tracking details directly from FedEx.

Flow:

FedEx Tracking Event
→ SurroundTrackingEventController.handleTrackingEvent()
→ Validate FDX_SIGNATURE and FDX_SUBSCRIPTION_ID headers
→ Generate expected signature using FedexTrackingEventHashCalculator.encode(requestBody)
→ Compare FedEx signature with expected signature
→ If valid, call publish(requestBody)
→ Parse payload using ObjectMapper
→ Create SurroundDataDTO and TrackingWebhookDTO
→ Call TrackingWebhookService.webhookPublisher()
→ TrackingWebhookServiceImpl.publish()
→ Serialize TrackingWebhookDTO using ObjectMapper
→ MessagingPublisher.publish()
→ Publish message to GCP topic advship-tracking-fedex-surround
→ Tracking Data Processor consumes and processes the message

Key Points

The Surround Edge Service acts as the entry point for shipment/tracking details received from FedEx.

The v1/api/surround-tracking-events API is specifically exposed for FedEx to send the shipment details.

Requests are validated for the required FedEx headers and signature before publishing.

The incoming FedEx payload is transformed into the application's TrackingWebhookDTO.

The validated event is published to GCP Pub/Sub for further processing.

Unknown fields in the FedEx payload are ignored using FAIL_ON_UNKNOWN_PROPERTIES = false.



---

Tracking Data Processor Listener

Once the message is published to the GCP topic, the Tracking Data Processor consumes the message using TrackingWebhookFedexListener.

Flow:

TrackingWebhookFedexListener.configure()
→ Subscribe using MessagingSubscriber
→ receiveMessage(PubsubMessage)
→ Read Pub/Sub message payload
→ Deserialize payload into FedexWrapper
→ Extract TrackingFedexDTO using wrapper.getJsonPayload()
→ Generate GCS file path using Billing Account Number + Tracking Number + Timestamp
→ If Cold Storage is enabled → Upload complete FedEx payload to GCS bucket
→ Check Global Subscription configuration
→ If enabled → RetryableMessageProcessor.processMessage()
→ If disabled → TrackingWebhookFedexPublisher.trackingFedexPublisher()
→ Continue with shipment processing

Key Points

TrackingWebhookFedexListener is the Pub/Sub consumer for FedEx Surround tracking events.

The listener converts the incoming message into FedexWrapper and extracts the actual TrackingFedexDTO.

The Billing Account Number and Tracking Number are used to construct the GCS cold-storage path.

When Cold Storage is enabled, the original FedEx payload is stored in GCS for archival/reprocessing purposes.

Processing behavior is controlled by the Global Subscription Enabled configuration:

Enabled: Uses the newer RetryableMessageProcessor flow.

Disabled: Uses the existing TrackingWebhookFedexPublisher flow.




---

Final Data Persistence

After the FedEx data is consumed and processed by the Tracking Data Processor, the application internally calls the Tracking Resource Application through its POST API.

The processed shipment information is ultimately persisted in the shipment table.

Flow:

FedEx
→ Surround Edge Service
→ GCP Pub/Sub – advship-tracking-fedex-surround
→ TrackingWebhookFedexListener.receiveMessage()
→ TrackingFedexDTO
→ RetryableMessageProcessor / TrackingWebhookFedexPublisher
→ POST API to Tracking Resource Application
→ Shipment processing
→ shipment table
→ Available for Beacon tracking/history

Key Points

The Tracking Resource Application is responsible for the final shipment persistence.

The Tracking Data Processor internally invokes the Tracking Resource Application through its POST API.

The processed FedEx shipment information is stored in the shipment table.

This persisted data is subsequently available to Beacon for tracking and history views.



---

Shipment Creation / Storage

The Tracking Resource Application uses shipmentBook as the aspect name for saving new shipment information.

The overall persistence flow can therefore be represented as:

Tracking Data Processor
→ POST API to Tracking Resource Application
→ shipmentBook aspect
→ Save/Process Shipment
→ shipment table

Key Points

shipmentBook is the aspect used for saving new shipment information.

FedEx Non-Navigator shipment data eventually reaches the shipment persistence layer through this flow.

The shipment table acts as the persistence layer for the shipment information.



---

Shipment Fetching / Tracking Details

Once the shipment data is stored, Beacon retrieves shipment information through the Tracking API.

API

POST
v1/api/tracking

The API is exposed through the advship-tracking-api application.

Flow

v1/api/tracking
→ TrackingDetailsController
→ TrackingDetailsServiceImpl
→ Internal call to /tracking/entities
→ advship-tracking-resource
→ trackingDetails aspect
→ Fetch shipment information
→ Return shipment data to Tracking API
→ Beacon

Key Points

v1/api/tracking is the API used for fetching shipment/tracking information.

TrackingDetailsController acts as the API entry point.

TrackingDetailsServiceImpl handles the service-level processing.

The Tracking API internally calls /tracking/entities in advship-tracking-resource.

trackingDetails is the aspect used for fetching shipment information.

The response contains the shipment data required by Beacon's Tracking/History views.



