Non-Navigator Shipment Filtering

The shipment-fetching flow also supports filtering based on the isNonNavigator() flag.

When isNonNavigator() = false:

→ Fetches all applicable shipments, including both Navigator and Non-Navigator shipments.

When isNonNavigator() = true:

→ Fetches only Non-Navigator shipments.

Flow:

v1/api/tracking
→ TrackingDetailsController
→ TrackingDetailsServiceImpl
→ /tracking/entities
→ trackingDetails aspect
→ Check isNonNavigator()
→ false → Navigator + Non-Navigator shipments
→ true → Non-Navigator shipments only

Key Points

isNonNavigator() determines whether the query should return only Non-Navigator shipments or all applicable shipments.

False allows both Navigator and Non-Navigator shipment data to be returned.

True restricts the result to Non-Navigator shipment data.

This filtering is important for supporting the Include Unverified Data functionality in Beacon.



